# This project is plain HTML/CSS/JS with no build step or server, so the
# browser cannot read a .env file directly — that only works with a bundler
# (Vite, Next.js, etc.) or a backend process.
#
# For this version, copy config.example.js to config.js and put your key
# there instead (config.js is git-ignored, same effect as a .env file).
#
# This .env.example is kept for reference and for Version 2, where a small
# backend/proxy could read the key from a real environment variable so it
# never ships to the browser at all. See "Future improvements" in README.md.

WEATHER_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
